🐶 Dog Years Project
📖 Story

Dogs age faster than humans. To compare their growth:

The first 2 years of a dog’s life = 10.5 dog years each

Each year after that = 4 dog years

So, if you’re 8 years old:

First 2 years → 2 × 10.5 = 21 dog years

Remaining 6 years → 6 × 4 = 24 dog years

Total → 45 dog years

Instead of doing the math by hand, we’ll use JavaScript to write a program that converts human age into dog years.

-------

📝 Tasks (10 Steps)

Set your age

Create a variable myAge equal to your age (as a number).

Add a comment explaining the line.

Start with early years

Create a variable earlyYears with the value 2.

Comment: this represents the first 2 human years.

Convert early years to dog years

Multiply earlyYears by 10.5 using the *= operator.

Calculate later years

Subtract 2 from myAge and store the result in laterYears.

Comment: this represents the remaining human years after the first 2.

Convert later years to dog years

Multiply laterYears by 4 using the *= operator.

Add a comment explaining this calculation.

(Optional Check)

console.log(earlyYears);

console.log(laterYears);

Confirm the numbers look correct.

Total age in dog years

Add earlyYears + laterYears → store in myAgeInDogYears.

Comment: this is your full age in dog years.

Format your name

Store your name as a string in myName.

Call .toLowerCase() on it.

Comment: .toLowerCase() makes your name all lowercase.

Output the result

Use console.log() with string interpolation:

console.log(`My name is ${myName}. I am ${myAge} years old in human years, which is ${myAgeInDogYears} years old in dog years.`);


Comment: this prints the final sentence with your details.

Test with other ages

Change myAge and re-run.

(Extra practice: try rewriting without the *= operator).
